# fixedbugs, defect 568, lane b18-guard, 2026-10-10 (panel 205's R3).
#
# SYMPTOM: a switch the C library reads once, at its first header
# (`_GNU_SOURCE` at glibc's `features.h`, `_POSIX_C_SOURCE` at Darwin's
# `sys/cdefs.h`), did nothing from a header of the program's own named by a
# module's first group: the unit read `<stdint.h>` and `<math.h>` before any
# group, and on Linux arm64 `sched_getcpu` was refused as undeclared. This
# header says so itself, on every platform: it stops the build where either
# was read before it.
#
# FIX: `heroes_runtime.h` spells its integer types from clang's builtins and
# reads no header of the C library; a unit includes its groups' headers
# first and the compiler's own after them, `hero_os.h` reading `<stdint.h>`
# and `<math.h>` (`runtime/heroes_standard.h`), so a switch a module's first
# group sets stands before every header of the library.

extern "fixedbugs-568-the-first-group-s-header-is-read-before-the-c-library.h"
    function answer() -> i64

function main()
    print(answer())
